<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31947" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκεῖθεν</span></b> , poet. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεῖθεν</span></b>  (the only form used by <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i>, also in Trag. where metre requires) : 
			Aeol.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κήνοθεν</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Alc.
			86
		</span></i> : 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηνῶθεν</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Ar.
			<u>Ach.</u>
			754
		</span></i> ; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηνῶθε</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Theoc.
			3.10
		</span></i>:—Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>from that place, thence,</i>
			opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκεῖσε,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				490
			</span></i>, etc. ; of a person, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τἀκεῖθεν εἰ ποθούμεθα</span>”
				<i>on his part,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					632
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ἐ. ἄγγελος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					619b
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ σκῆπτρον ἐ. παραλαβόντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					6.181b
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκεῖ, οἱ ἐ.</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.62
			</span></i> : c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὐκεῖθεν ἄλσους</span>
			<i>on yon side of</i> the grove, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				505
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕζοντο τὸ κεῖθεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					1411
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> by
			attraction for 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκεῖσε, βῆναι κεῖθεν ὅθενπερ ἥκει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					1227
				</span></i>
			 codd. (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>thence, from that fact,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γνοίη δ᾽ ἄν τις ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					12.224
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				45.48
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> of
			Time, <i>thenceforward,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				15.234
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἤδη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					54.25
				</span></i>
			.</div>
